/-!
# Atlas V-03: complex-valued parameter calculus (joint smoothness, interchange, frame derivatives)

Complex-valued analogues of IV's `Atlas/EinsteinMaxwell/Variation/Joint.lean` (which treats real-valued families):
for a family `Φ : ℝ → Pt n → ℂ` that is jointly `C^∞` in `(ε, y)` on an open `W ⊆ ℝ × ℝⁿ`

* `contDiffOn_cpdC_joint`: coordinate derivatives `cpdC i (Φ ε) y` are again jointly `C^∞`;
* `hasDerivAt_param_of_jointC`: `ε ↦ Φ ε y` has a genuine derivative at every point of `W`;
* `hasDerivAt_cpdC_param` (**interchange**): `d/dε|_{ε₀} cpdC i (Φ ε) x = cpdC i ψ x` whenever `ψ y` is the
  genuine parameter derivative of `ε ↦ Φ ε y` on the open slice (symmetry of the second derivative);
* `contDiffOn_deriv_slice`: the parameter derivative `y ↦ ∂_ε Φ(ε₀, y)` is `C^∞` on the slice;
* `hasDerivAt_fdir_param`: the first variation of a frame derivative keeps the frame-variation term,
  `δ(D_A f) = Σ_μ b_A^μ ∂_μ f₀ + D_A δf`;
* complex matrix determinant / adjugate / left-inverse smoothness (copies of IV's real versions).

No new geometric object is defined here. -/

